050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1031 "Measures of Segments" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1033 1379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050563 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "53e39f98-0b09-5a55-8519-b9bae786a859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1031 "Properties of Congruence" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1033 502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050655 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5ce0b2bd-c517-5f90-9595-e2b26bd69b30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110374 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110374 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AC=BD$\n2. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n3. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110374 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d23b33d-46ad-56af-853c-353c306c7af0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110374 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5$. So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110375 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2554" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110375 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the line segments shown below are congruent?\n\n![](images/fe/fea89643ee848c5cce4ea9844da71fae26f4799c4dbbe5795086a5365fbf3ec9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110375 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a53bc0ac-2deb-53f9-a4cf-2ac02b903cd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110375 #edb/ref 1074 "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110376 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110376 #edb/ref 1071 "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true?\n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n1. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n2. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n3. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110376 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5cdb5e0-0ea7-5a96-81d4-0b53e2ad2f9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110376 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}$.\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}$.\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}$.\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD}$, and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110741 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110741 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110741 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Congruent Segments on a Number Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110741 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110741 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "dee17b1d-686f-5817-b7dd-bf5b0bbd3da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Congruent Line Segments on a Grid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110742 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cb023488-e5ec-5d04-9cc2-b40db799887c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110743 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110743 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110743 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1045 "Congruent Segments" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110834 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c06b4e33-1b3c-55b4-883e-d93402ee309a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111715 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111715 #edb/ref 1061 8703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5c755862-dc82-5232-8df9-c287c6e24622" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111716 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111716 #edb/ref 1061 8706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111716 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "542b00a8-274a-5911-bbce-1439d6e3509f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111716 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111717 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111717 #edb/ref 1061 8707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111717 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99d401ca-55c5-5d3a-b140-7959973804ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111717 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111718 #edb/ref 1061 8709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111718 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f764618b-d970-5154-af8e-e3fd3e9fc7f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111718 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111834 #edb/ref 1064 "When two line segments have the same length, they are **congruent** segments. To indicate that the line segments $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ are congruent we write\n$\\overline{AB} \\:\\:{\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\cong}}\\:\\: \\overline{CD}$,\nand we use special marks like in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d7fd26fce7dce67fa57769db3e96be503051be5c7d2c7714ed48927547d5165.png)\n\nWe can also write\n\n$$\nAB \\:{\\color{blue}=}\\: CD\n$$\n\nwhich means that the measure of $\\overline{AB}$ is equal to the measure of $\\overline{CD}$.\n\n**Watch out!** The equation\n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} = \\overline{CD}\n$$\n\nis only true when both $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ correspond to the same exact segment. When the segments are distinct, we should use the symbol $\\cong$ to represent that the two segments are separate but that they have the same length." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111834 #edb/ref 1065 2164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111834 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a565176c-749f-56b7-aa7c-4d200187c50f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111834 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
